# Finding 14 (second half) — the palette box re-anchors as you type.
# `picker.placeWith` (src/ui/picker.zig) derives the box height from the
# filtered item count and `overlay.place` re-centres it (ui.picker_position
# defaults to .center), so the whole box slides DOWN the screen as the list
# shrinks. VS Code keeps the palette put and only the list shrinks.
# The activity-bar margin differs per row, so the row the top border sits on
# is identifiable: it opens on a blank-margin row ("   |"), and after a query
# it has moved onto the row whose margin carries the 󰎒 glyph.
# Correct behaviour: the box stays where it opened.
# width: 120
# height: 40
write a.txt hello
open a.txt
command palette
expect screen contains "   │           ┌ Command palette "
type toggle wrap
expect screen contains "toggle wrap"
expect screen contains "   │           ┌ Command palette "
